    <bpmn:process id="W_W4920" name="W4920. Multi-Entity Program Governance &amp; Cross-Company Standards" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Program launch (W4913); 5-entity consistency; entity/structure change
Frequency: Annual + on entity/structure change
Volume: 5 entities (Depot/Logistics/Digital Commerce/Property/Holdings) × program governance
Owner: Uniform &amp; Workwear Program Manager / HR Shared Services (VS-103/VS-72) / Legal
Participants: HR (VS-19/VS-103), Shared Services (VS-72), Brand (VS-14), Finance (VS-17), Legal (VS-100)
Source: workflow W4920 — Multi-Entity Program Governance &amp; Cross-Company Standards</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4920_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4920_Lane1" name="Program Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4920_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4920_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4920_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4920_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4920_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4920_Start3" name="Program launch (W4913); 5-entity consistency; entity/structure change">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4920_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4920_Task4" name="Set the cross-entity program governance: group uniform/PPE standards applied…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Set the cross-entity program governance: group uniform/PPE standards applied across the 5 entities, entity-specific exceptions (Logistics DC hi-vis, Property facilities, Digital Commerce HQ), the centralized procurement/standards vs decentralized issuance model, and the approval matrix for entity variance
Responsible (R): Program Manager / Brand / HR / Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO / COO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4920_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4920_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4920_Task5" name="Manage cross-company consistency &amp; chargeback (VS-72): central procurement with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Manage cross-company consistency &amp; chargeback (VS-72): central procurement with entity allocation, the cost chargeback across entities, consistent standards/branding, and entity-specific PPE requirements (e.g., Logistics DC vs Depot store)
Responsible (R): Program Manager / Shared Services / Finance
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4920_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4920_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4920_Task6" name="Govern via shared services (VS-103/VS-72): central standards/vendor/quality…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Govern via shared services (VS-103/VS-72): central standards/vendor/quality with decentralized store/entity issuance, report entity compliance (W4930) and cost (W4929), and manage the intercompany chargeback settlement (links VS-72)
Responsible (R): Program Manager / Shared Services / Finance
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4920_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4920_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4920_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4920_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4920_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-132 (ensure PPE issuance &amp; DOLE compliance.) | - CTL-737: group standards + entity exceptions; centralized procurement; fair cost chargeback (VS-72)
Owner: Uniform &amp; Workwear Program Manager / HR Shared Services (VS-103/VS-72) / Legal</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
